      "content": "I noticed your comment about the enzyme being a \"masterful little creature.\" While I'll keep the kinetics technical, I actually want to address the biological impact for the students. \n\nThe onset of the irritation from the propanethial S-oxide feels quite sudden and almost \"aggressive\" to the sensory nerves. Can you describe the biochemical mechanism of this sudden onset? I'm interested in why the sensation feels so sharp and seemingly \"unprovoked\" once the gas hits the moisture on the eye.",
