      "role": "user",
      "content": "It's an interesting comparison, though I'd prefer to stay on the neurobiology of the response. \n\nYou mentioned the sensory nerves acting like \"vigilant sentinels.\" Could you elaborate on the specific signaling pathway? I want to explain to the students exactly how the sudden chemical change in the tear film triggers the nociceptors, and why the human body perceives this specific chemical interaction as such a sharp, biting pain rather than a dull ache.",
      "source": "evaluator"
